    <!-- Everything a viewer reads, so a language is one file (values-tl is Tagalog). The English
         is what the code used to say, word for word. Not here on purpose: the Signal & TS
         Analyzer, the Developers screen and the USB probe (technical tools; the analyzer also
         colours its log by matching English words), the licence texts, log lines, and the remote
         key names DATA / BACK / OK / CC / REC, which are printed that way on the remotes and in
         the broadcasts. opendtv/TRANSLATING.md has the word list for adding a screen or a language.

         Strings with two spaces in a row are in quotes: a resource collapses runs of spaces
         otherwise, and the gaps are part of the layout. -->

